 { Here is a similar case. Anybody with basic endgame skills should find White's first move here! } 1. { -KEY- } Ra3 $1 { The rook behind the passed pawn. } ( { Obviously, } 1. a6 $2 Ra4 { would let Black achieve the same thing, with increased drawing chances. } ) 
Rb7 2. a6 Ra7 3. Ra5 $1 { A move similar to Lasker's 3 Rf4 in the previous example. Black's king is now restricted, and the rest is easy. } Kf6 4. g4 Ke7 5. Kg3 Kd6 6. Kf4 Kc7 7. Ke5 Kd7 ( { Or } 7... Kb6 8. Ra1 Rg7 9. a7 $1 { and the g-pawn decides. } ) 
8. g5 Ke7 9. g6 Kf8 10. Kxe6 Ke8 11. g7 Rxg7 12. a7 Rg6+ 13. Kf5 
