 { Black is seemingly in big danger, but Anand survived by transferring his rook to the back of the passed pawn. } 1... { -KEY- } Rh1 $1 ( { Black shouldn't play } 1... h5 $2 { , as after } 2. Ke3 hxg4 3. Rxg4 $1 { , a symmetric kingside pawn structure arises, which means he is lost - Anand. This thesis is easy to understand, since contrary to an asymmetric structure (e.g. pawns on g4 and f7), Black can't easily swap off those pawns, nor create a passed pawn. } ) 
